---
import Command from '../Command.astro';
---

<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Tooling</span>
      <h2>The whole toolchain, in one command.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Everything ships with Haxeon and works the same in the editor and on the command line. No
        plugins to assemble.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid four tools">
      <div>
        <div class="titled">
          <svg class="ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M4 5h16v10H9l-5 4z"></path><path d="M10.5 8l-2 2 2 2M13.5 8l2 2-2 2"></path>
          </svg><h3>Language server</h3>
        </div><Command command="haxeon lsp" /><p class="detail">
          Completion, go to definition, diagnostics as you type. The VS Code extension uses it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="titled">
          <svg class="ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M4 12h5M13 12h7"></path><circle cx="11" cy="12" r="2.5"></circle><path
              d="M17 9l3 3-3 3"
            >
            </path>
          </svg><h3>Debugger</h3>
        </div><div class="cmd">Debug Adapter Protocol</div><p class="detail">
          Breakpoints, stepping, watchpoints, logpoints and exception breaks, even across a live
          edit. On x64 Linux, Windows and Intel macOS.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="titled">
          <svg class="ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M4 6h16M4 10h10M4 14h16M4 18h8"></path>
          </svg><h3>Formatter and linter</h3>
        </div><div class="cmd">haxeon fmt · haxeon lint</div><p class="detail">
          One house style, and checks that know your types.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="titled">
          <svg class="ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M4 20h16M7 20v-6M11 20V7M15 20v-9M19 20v-4"></path>
          </svg><h3>Profiler</h3>
        </div><Command command="haxeon run --profile" /><p class="detail">
          A timeline of your running program, opened in Perfetto or in VS Code.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="titled">
          <svg class="ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
            <rect x="4" y="5" width="16" height="14" rx="2"></rect><path d="M8.5 12l2.5 2.5 4.5-5"
            ></path>
          </svg><h3>Build and test</h3>
        </div><div class="cmd">haxeon build · check · test</div><p class="detail">
          Incremental builds through a compile server that stays warm.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="titled">
          <svg class="ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M12 3l8 4.5v9L12 21l-8-4.5v-9z"></path><path d="M4 7.5l8 4.5 8-4.5M12 12v9"
            ></path>
          </svg><h3>Packages</h3>
        </div><Command command="haxeon add ui" /><p class="detail">
          Version ranges and a lockfile, with the first-party packages in the SDK's registry.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="titled">
          <svg class="ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M9 3v5M15 3v5M7 8h10v3a5 5 0 0 1-10 0z"></path><path d="M12 16v5"></path>
          </svg><h3>C and C++ bindings</h3>
        </div><Command command="haxeon ffi import" /><p class="detail">Bindings generated from headers.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="titled">
          <svg class="ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M3 12h4l2-5 4 10 2-5h6"></path>
          </svg><h3>Setup check</h3>
        </div><Command command="haxeon doctor" /><p class="detail">
          Names what is missing and the command that installs it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .tools > div {
    border-top: 2px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5);
    padding-top: var(--hx-space-4);
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--hx-space-2);
    align-content: start;
    min-width: 0;
  }
</style>
